"_about": "The two tables that used to sit at the foot of glossary.js (GLOSSARY_PLACES, GLOSSARY_MAP_COUNTRY) — an OFFLINE input since Atlas v2 Phase 5, no longer shipped. points: glossary slug -> [lon, lat], the Wikipedia article's primary coordinate (31 terms that name a point). countries: glossary slug -> the name the retired v1 globe used for the country the term names (181 terms). Read by migrate-places.js (the points, to resolve them against the registry) and build-glossary-places.js (both, to write atlas/data/glossary-places.js). To give a NEW term the Atlas pin, add it here and run node .claude/migrate-places.js (docs/atlas-v2-phase5-plan.md §5, docs/atlas-v2-design.md §2.8). reviewed (2026-11-28): glossary slug -> registry id, a term tagged a place whose title or alias is the name of a registry row, each pair read by hand (a wrong namesake, a continent, a biome left out); a polity id gives a window only, never a pin.",
